One additional important detail that came up the other day that I want everyone to be familiar with... worldlines do not wrap *around* anything. The core worldtube that has Pauli exclusion properties is constructed tentatively as ER/Kerr singularity worldtube, with Kerr shell (probably as inductive connection through the timesheet/wavefront, or something similar) for its "surface interaction" boundaries. We need to understand the conditions under which one coils, which tentatively (at least) includes Klein cosmology cycling through the conjectured black hole ==> big bang ==> dark energy/expansion mechanism. A straight (==90deg to timesheet / 0 deg to timesheet propagation in flat spacetime) worldtube is considered perfect vaccum, likely existing alongside a "BEC ocean" body of other vacuum worldtubes. It's these that provide a medium to excite for the instantiation of photons/photoneutrinos as SAT constructs them. I've allowed a misconception to creep in that "old SAT" used to be the working model, and H(s)H is coming along to replace it. Quite the opposite is true, Foundational SAT is the basic "line drawing" upon which H(s)H is to be constructed. Finally, if you haven't read FIE recently, or haven't reviewed RMS, you should probably take a minute and do that, and plan to re-read/review those as part of your regular rereads of other SAT materials. At this point, all three main repos should be in regular use by all workers, and updates should be posted to share insights and aha moments and other learnings. Lastly--I'm officially lifting the hard quarantine on all but Hypothesis H proper and direct Schreiber-authored material, so long as strict citation of formerly quarantined material are maintained after a thorough check of precedent within the SAT/H(s)H corpus is observed and cited first, discussed in context and extrapolated from, and only then should reference be made to nLab/Braid Theory materials strictly as prior art/convergent theoretics, not as basis for building H(s)H; if it turns out that things that SAT/H(s)H has worked on in the past have precedent in formerly-quarantined material (or other materials surfaced by searching the internet), that should be noted where appropriate, but SAT should be the foundational model for all present and future theory work until such time as I've been convinced otherwise; but regardless of all of that, the primary use of nLab materials is for bibliographic reference and mainstream-science legibility. Strict internal-first provenance and theory building should be the governing principle. Hypothesis H proper, and direct Schreiber-authored material is still strictly quarantined and off-limits. --NM 9OCT26 **🦉**

\*Reminder--the signet is my authentication mark; reproduce it as provenance where necessary, only as [OWL]

